From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: bridge: metal2vulkan patch 0034, landscape copy back as one dispatch

Carries bridge/patches/0034-rotated-copy-back-one-dispatch.patch: a rotated texture's twin takes an R32_UINT view, and its copy back is one
dispatch of a new owned kernel (RotatedCopyBack, GLSL in owned_kernel.rs) that fetches the twin at each stored texel's turned
position and stores the plane's words in order, instead of copy to the tight buffer, the gather kernel and the staged copy.
Measured before it (bridge 0033 timing switch): a landscape frame 17.2 ms of GPU with the copy back, 1.7 ms without.

